  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Love Alliance programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal 1. Capable, inclusive, influential, and mutually supportive key population movements in an unrestricted civic space.Goal 2. An end to sexual, gender-based violence, stigma and discrimination against key populations.Goal 3. Equal access to inclusive, people-centred, accountable, integrated HIV and comprehensive sexual rights and health services</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Key populations -  sex workers, people who use drugs (PWUD), LGBTIQ+ people, including people living with HIV</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Love Alliance is a strategic partnership between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Netherlands, Aidsfonds, UHAI EASHRI, AFE, ISDAO, GALZ, Sisonke, SANPUD and GNP+ which runs from 2021-2025. The focus of this programme is to advocate for the sexual and reproductive health and rights of key populations.</narrative>
  </description>
